      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We should finalize a plan for a VTS test for this before submitting.\n\nThe current plan as discussed with @armellel@google.com is to run the trusty tests as VTS tests in a separate VM.\nI am in the process of writing trusty tests for the AuthMgr TA that implements this AIDL interface, to test the e2e protocol (WIP CL topic for the TA: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/q/topic:%22authmgr-be-ta%22 which integrates the reference implementation in the CL topic: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/q/topic:%22authmgr-core%22). \n\n\n\u003e  Ideally we can have a VTS test in Android that would run against binder services or TEE services serving the same instance\n\nAFAIU, writing a VTS test in Android requires adding a HAL service in Android that routes the requests to the TEE service. I am not sure if we want to add a HAL service in Android for this.\n\n\n\u003e could we add a normal VTS test here which asserts that this interface is not implemented via binder, because we don\u0027t have test coverage for that?\n\nSure, I will add a VTS test here which asserts that this interface is not implemented via binder. \n(I suppose that I need to call `check_interface` (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/libs/binder/rust/src/service.rs;l\u003d185) and asset that it returns `StatusCode::NAME_NOT_FOUND`)",
      "parentUuid": "3a2ae048_c292f00b",
      "revId": "7e1dcbe6c0dfb33f85f040e44868f20183d33612",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
